# Hector Bulgarini SBP Milestone 1 Review

The SBP Milestone 1 review comments can be found under the comments with the following format:

```
    /// <HB SBP Milestone 1 Review:
    /// ...
    /// commments
    /// ...
    /// HB SBP>
```


## Common Good Parathread decision

There may not be a major issue if there is no rush to deploy this chain. However, parathread development work has not yet begun, so if the goal for this project is to deploy it as a common good parathread, this could be a blocker. 

## Scope of the parachain 

During the call, it was mentioned that the current state of this parachain does not add value because of how the reserve-based transfer process works. This is because when assets are transferred to the DEX parachain for swapping carbon assets, they are sent back to the reserve parachain and then to the target parachain, with this parachain not doing anything with the assets received. This is a valid concern and to justify its development as a parachain, additional logic needs to be included. Doing some brainstorming, this parachain could act as the trusted parachain from the DEX parachain perspective, enabling it to execute a Transact XCM instruction and automate the swap process.

## XCM configuration

I would suggest a review of the XCM configuration for this parachain, as there seem to be some misunderstandings regarding the roles of reserves and teleporting (as explained in the comments).

This is a matter of taste, but I find vertical spacing to be crucial for readability.

I find it difficult to match what docstring goes with what element in this:

```rust
enum Meme {
  /// foo
  Badger,
  /// bar
  Mushroom,
  /// baz
  Snake,
}
```

While this is clear:
```rust
enum Meme {
  /// foo
  Badger,

  /// bar
  Mushroom,

  /// baz
  Snake,
}
```

similarly, I find it good practice to have a blank line before each new type declaration or `impl` block.

